# Nothing in this directory is copied into the image — the Dockerfile installs
# Wringer from PyPI — so the build context exists only to be handed to the
# builder. Keeping it small keeps builds fast, and keeping evidence bundles
# and .env files out of it means they are never uploaded anywhere by accident.
#
# What is deliberately NOT excluded: pyproject.toml, src/, README.md and
# LICENSE. If the Dockerfile is ever pointed at the local tree instead of
# PyPI, a source build needs all four, and an ignore rule is a confusing way
# to discover that.

# git history and CI definitions
.git
.gitignore
.github

# local environments, caches, build output
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
dist
build

# evidence bundles: local by design, and they carry captured gate output
.wringer
.wringer.example

# secrets
.env
.env.*

# tests and scratch — not needed to build or run the image
tests
scratch
tmp
*.tmp
*.log

# editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
